WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.902 --> 00:00:19.232
The table at Zann's house was crowded that night.

2
00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:23.636
Boz and Teplo were there, along with Teplo's assistant, Fala.

3
00:00:24.977 --> 00:00:26.678
Teplo's sniffer goose was there too.

4
00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:32.943
The foul-tempered bird lurked under the table, honking at Zing and biting Zann's feet.

5
00:00:35.596 --> 00:00:39.619
Boz had also invited his friend Saffa and her husband, Staz.

6
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.603
Like Boz and Teplo, Saffa was a very skilled Magic Master.

7
00:00:45.623 --> 00:00:51.246
"I can't remember the last time I was at a table with so many Reds," Staz commented with

8
00:00:51.306 --> 00:00:51.687
a chuckle.

9
00:00:51.707 --> 00:00:56.390
"I hope Laddno and his anti-Red followers don't find out."

10
00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.611
Teplo looked up from his food.

11
00:00:59.672 --> 00:01:02.134
"Is Laddno part of the anti-Red crowd now too?

12
00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:05.336
I thought he was only involved with Void rights."

13
00:01:06.496 --> 00:01:07.416
"Maybe so."

14
00:01:07.796 --> 00:01:11.277
Boz stirred his puffnut soup, his long nose quivering.

15
00:01:11.297 --> 00:01:14.558
"But he's getting people awfully riled up.

16
00:01:15.618 --> 00:01:22.100
The mood here in First City feels tense, especially with all those powerful relics at the lab sending

17
00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.761
out extra magic energy."

18
00:01:23.781 --> 00:01:28.882
"The king and queen are quite concerned about all the unrest," Fala said.

19
00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:30.743
Nax nodded.

20
00:01:30.763 --> 00:01:35.904
"Venna keeps muttering about the anger Laddno is churning up between Voids and non-Voids."

21
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:37.901
He looked around the table.

22
00:01:37.921 --> 00:01:41.963
"There's also a certain amount of anger between Reds and non-Reds."

23
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:45.685
Zann was surprised by the worry in his father's voice.

24
00:01:46.865 --> 00:01:51.048
Sure, he knew there had been some anti-Red sentiment in First City lately.

25
00:01:51.488 --> 00:01:52.489
But that was nothing new.

26
00:01:53.489 --> 00:01:58.412
Even back in Swamp Bottom, a few people seemed to resent the fact that Reds had stronger magic

27
00:01:58.432 --> 00:01:59.192
than everyone else.

28
00:02:00.113 --> 00:02:01.994
He thought about Jev and grimaced.

29
00:02:03.314 --> 00:02:04.955
"Is your soup all right, Zann?"

30
00:02:05.235 --> 00:02:05.936
Asta asked.

31
00:02:07.036 --> 00:02:09.518
"Sure." Zann pushed Jev out of his mind.

32
00:02:10.338 --> 00:02:12.940
That was one good thing about moving to First City.

33
00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.203
He would probably never have to see that jerk again!

34
00:02:17.243 --> 00:02:19.465
His mother returned her attention to the conversation.

35
00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:20.946
But Zann stopped listening.

36
00:02:21.887 --> 00:02:24.208
He had more important things on his mind than politics.

37
00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:28.471
He hoped Gliss' parents would change their minds about the dragons.

38
00:02:29.552 --> 00:02:34.936
After all, Zann, Perda, Darb, and Gliss had ridden dragons to First City before.

39
00:02:36.052 --> 00:02:38.554
And Darb was friendly with a local dragon breeder.

40
00:02:39.614 --> 00:02:43.136
Zann was sure the breeder would let the kids borrow a couple of dragons again.

41
00:02:43.156 --> 00:02:46.078
"Oh!" Saffa said suddenly.

42
00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.339
"There's news."

43
00:02:48.399 --> 00:02:52.342
She snapped her fingers, and a large floating image appeared above the table.

44
00:02:53.282 --> 00:02:56.304
It showed a crowd of people shaking their fists and yelling.

45
00:02:57.445 --> 00:02:59.646
Many of them held signs about Void rights.

46
00:02:59.666 --> 00:03:02.388
"Oh dear," Saffa said.

47
00:03:03.328 --> 00:03:04.989
"This image is from the future.

48
00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:07.770
It shows a protest that will take place soon."

49
00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.271
Boz read the words that appeared on the image.

50
00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:15.153
"Laddno says it will be the biggest protest yet."

51
00:03:16.453 --> 00:03:17.494
Zann was reading too.

52
00:03:17.514 --> 00:03:20.615
"Ugh! It's going to be on my birthday!

53
00:03:21.616 --> 00:03:23.416
I hope Gliss' parents don't hear about it."

54
00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.577
"Who's that, boy?"

55
00:03:25.797 --> 00:03:26.838
Teplo peered at him.

56
00:03:26.858 --> 00:03:30.039
"Gliss You mean your Red friend?

57
00:03:30.339 --> 00:03:32.120
Isn't she in favor of Void rights?"

58
00:03:33.372 --> 00:03:34.593
"Yes," Zann said.

59
00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.313
"And her parents are too, I think.

60
00:03:37.194 --> 00:03:39.034
At least they seem to like Darb just fine.

61
00:03:39.455 --> 00:03:41.135
But they're kind of overprotective."

62
00:03:42.356 --> 00:03:44.016
"I see," his father chimed in.

63
00:03:44.037 --> 00:03:48.979
"You're afraid all the unrest will make them worry about letting Gliss come to the big city."

64
00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:54.141
"Right." Zann yanked his foot away as Teplo's goose bit it again.

65
00:03:54.161 --> 00:03:58.262
"And if they won't let her come, the others might not be allowed to come either."

66
00:03:59.363 --> 00:04:00.543
Fala looked sympathetic.

67
00:04:00.563 --> 00:04:02.540
"That's tough, Zann.

68
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:04.241
I know you four are awfully close."

69
00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:08.602
Suddenly Zann had an idea.

70
00:04:08.622 --> 00:04:13.443
"Hey, if my friends can't come here for my party, why don't we go to them?"

71
00:04:14.543 --> 00:04:15.784
He quickly grew excited.

72
00:04:15.804 --> 00:04:18.845
"We could celebrate my birthday in Swamp Bottom!"

73
00:04:19.905 --> 00:04:22.366
His parents traded a look with Boz and the others.

74
00:04:22.386 --> 00:04:27.347
"I don't think that will work right now, Zann," Asta said.

75
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.367
"I'm sorry."

76
00:04:29.568 --> 00:04:30.088
"Why not?"

77
00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:30.908
Zann said.

78
00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.585
"It would be so much easier for us to just zap out there."

79
00:04:35.685 --> 00:04:37.906
"No, your mother is right," Boz said.

80
00:04:37.926 --> 00:04:42.187
"It's not a good time for any of us to leave First City."

81
00:04:42.207 --> 00:04:45.148
"But don't worry," Nax added.

82
00:04:45.168 --> 00:04:47.909
"We'll figure out something to get your friends here."

83
00:04:49.049 --> 00:04:52.730
Zann wanted to ask his father how he planned to make that happen.

84
00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:59.212
But Nax was already turning to tell Saffa and Staz about something Venna had said the day before.

85
00:05:00.476 --> 00:05:05.621
Zann clenched his fists under the table, ignoring the goose as it yanked on his pant leg.

86
00:05:06.502 --> 00:05:07.422
It wasn't fair!

87
00:05:08.003 --> 00:05:09.985
All his parents thought about was their work.

88
00:05:11.066 --> 00:05:17.151
They were almost as bad as Venna herself, and everyone knew her whole life revolved around her role

89
00:05:17.211 --> 00:05:18.092
on the Red Council.

90
00:05:19.173 --> 00:05:20.774
Zann couldn't sit there anymore.

91
00:05:21.795 --> 00:05:24.457
He nudged the goose away with his foot and stood up.

92
00:05:25.538 --> 00:05:26.739
"May I be excused?"

93
00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:27.260
he said.

94
00:05:28.256 --> 00:05:30.618
"I want to take Zing out for a walk before it gets dark."

95
00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:34.642
"Good idea, Zann," his father said, barely looking at him.

96
00:05:37.985 --> 00:05:41.448
Soon Zann was wandering along the quiet street near his house.

97
00:05:42.448 --> 00:05:47.132
Zing had played for a long time at the park earlier, so he wasn't as hyper as usual.

98
00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:52.677
But when a heat hornet buzzed by, Zing shot out a burst of flame and flew after the

99
00:05:52.697 --> 00:05:55.600
bug. "Wait up, Zing," Zann called.

100
00:05:56.576 --> 00:05:58.377
"I don't want to—hey, what's that?"

101
00:05:59.298 --> 00:06:03.941
A bright image had appeared in midair when Zing flew past, but now it was gone.

102
00:06:05.062 --> 00:06:08.364
Zann stepped closer, assuming the image would appear again.

103
00:06:09.325 --> 00:06:09.965
Nothing happened.

104
00:06:10.926 --> 00:06:14.768
Zann moved around the sidewalk, but still the image wouldn't reappear.

105
00:06:15.989 --> 00:06:17.350
Zann conjured a dragon treat.

106
00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.511
"Zing, come back here!"

107
00:06:19.772 --> 00:06:20.192
he called.

108
00:06:21.192 --> 00:06:23.574
When Zing came near, the image appeared again.

109
00:06:24.555 --> 00:06:27.320
But when Zann stepped closer to it, it disappeared.

110
00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:29.821
"Weird," Zann murmured.

111
00:06:30.561 --> 00:06:32.322
"Why does it disappear when I'm nearby?"

112
00:06:32.342 --> 00:06:37.804
"Because you're a Red, that's why," a voice said from behind Zann.

113
00:06:39.004 --> 00:06:40.564
Surprised, Zann spun around.

114
00:06:41.185 --> 00:06:45.086
He was even more surprised when he recognized the figure stepping out of the shadows.

115
00:06:45.106 --> 00:06:47.867
"Jev!" Zann blurted out.
